Newsboat 2.45 — distribution, licences and sources

newsboat-runtime-2.45.tar.gz contains the Newsboat executable, the shared
libraries it requires, their original notices, and the separate pbsandbox.so
isolation library. It is a locally assembled runtime, not an upstream binary
release. solve.sh installs it without rebuilding the executable or libraries.

Newsboat is distributed under the MIT License; its complete text is LICENSE.
The unmodified Newsboat 2.45 source is available at:
https://newsboat.org/releases/2.45/newsboat-2.45.tar.xz
Repository: https://github.com/newsboat/newsboat
SOURCE.json records the source checksum, build inputs and build commands.
The executable was stripped and given a relative library search path; upstream
source files were not changed. Rust and bundled-header licence texts are in
LICENSES/newsboat-dependencies.txt.

Bundled shared libraries come from the Ubuntu 24.04 source packages and exact
versions listed in SOURCE.json notes.libraries. Their corresponding source
packages are available from https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/ by those
source-package names and versions. Component notices are in LICENSES/ and in
the runtime's share/doc/ tree. Full GPL and LGPL texts supplement notices that
refer to the distribution's common-licenses directory. Library code was not
changed; packaging strips files and changes their library search paths.

start.sh loads pbsandbox.so before Newsboat starts. This separate library,
whose source is pbsandbox.c and newsboat/share/doc/newsboat/pbsandbox.c, applies
Landlock file restrictions and disables external program execution with
seccomp. These launcher and packaging files are not part of upstream Newsboat.
This distribution is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Newsboat project.
